+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: format-duration-max-units
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, duration, formatting]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 1
+lane: light
+summary: "Optional max_units cap with half-up rounding and carry for format_duration"
+---
+
+# SPEC: format_duration `max_units`
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`format_duration` always prints every non-zero unit, so callers wanting a compact display ("about 2h") must truncate by hand and get rounding and carry wrong. An optional `max_units` parameter gives them a correct, rounded, bounded-length form.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+A caller can pass `max_units=n` (n >= 1) and receive at most n unit positions (d, h, m, s), counted from the largest non-zero unit, rounded half-up into the smallest kept position with carry. Without `max_units` the output is byte-identical to today.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: Default unchanged
+**Given** any non-negative integer `seconds`
+**When** `format_duration(seconds)` or `format_duration(seconds, max_units=None)` is called
+**Then** the result equals today's output (e.g. 5400 -> "1h30m", 0 -> "0s")
+
+### S2: Truncate with half-up rounding
+**Given** `seconds=5430` (1h30m30s)
+**When** `max_units=1` is passed
+**Then** the result is "2h"
+**And** `90, 1 -> "2m"`, `89, 1 -> "1m"`, `5399, 2 -> "1h30m"`
+
+### S3: Carry propagates upward
+**Given** `seconds=86399` (23h59m59s)
+**When** `max_units=2` is passed
+**Then** the result is "1d" (59s -> 60m -> 24h -> 1d)
+**And** `3599, 1 -> "1h"`
+
+### S4: A zero unit inside the window uses a position
+**Given** `seconds=3601` (1h0m1s)
+**When** `max_units=2` is passed
+**Then** the window is h,m; the 1s rounds down; the result is "1h"
+
+### S5: Zero and over-wide caps
+**Given** `seconds=0`, or `max_units` larger than the number of units present
+**When** `format_duration` is called with `max_units>=1`
+**Then** `0 -> "0s"`, and a wide cap returns the unbounded output unchanged
+
+### S6: Invalid max_units
+**Given** any `seconds`
+**When** `max_units` is 0 or negative
+**Then** `ValueError` is raised
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Type validation of `max_units` beyond `< 1` (bool/float behaviour unspecified).
+- Units larger than days, fractional seconds, changes to `parse_duration`, CLI flags.
+- Changing negative-`seconds` handling (still `ValueError`).
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | existing `tests/test_format.py` uses it |
+| Compatibility | `format_duration(seconds)` positional call unchanged | existing callers and tests |
+| Dependencies | none new | stdlib only |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none — adds an optional, defaulted keyword parameter; fully backward compatible and cheap to revert.
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `test_default_unchanged` |
+| S2 | unit | `test_max_units_rounding` |
+| S3 | unit | `test_max_units_carry` |
+| S4 | unit | `test_max_units_zero_in_window` |
+| S5 | unit | `test_max_units_zero_and_wide` |
+| S6 | unit | `test_max_units_invalid` |
+| S2-S4 (all inputs) | unit (property sweep) | `test_max_units_matches_round_then_format` |
+
+### AC-001: Default output unchanged
+Golden: `(5400,None)->"1h30m"`, `(0,None)->"0s"`, `(90061,None)->"1d1h1m1s"`. Source: the existing test file.
+
+### AC-002: Half-up rounding into smallest kept unit
+Golden table from the requester's examples (5430/1, 5399/2, 90/1, 89/1).
+
+### AC-003: Carry propagates upward
+Golden: 86399/2 -> "1d", 86399/1 -> "1d", 3599/1 -> "1h".
+
+### AC-004: Zero in window uses a position
+Golden: 3601/2 -> "1h", 7205/3 -> "2h5s", 3661/2 -> "1h1m".
+
+### AC-005: Zero and wide caps
+Golden: 0/1 -> "0s", 5400/4 -> "1h30m".
+
+### AC-006: Invalid max_units raises
+`max_units` of 0 and -1 raise `ValueError`.
+
+### AC-007: Agrees with round-then-format
+For all s in [0, 200000] and k in 1..5: let i be the index in (d,h,m,s) of the largest non-zero unit of s, `step = UNITS[unit at min(i+k-1, 3)]`, `r = (s + step//2)//step*step`; then `format_duration(s, k) == format_duration(r)`.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Step 0: not skipped (new parameter, rounding semantics are not title-obvious). Lane `light`: one file (`timeparse/format.py`) plus tests, one session, no irreversible decision.
+- Round 1 (no question tool available; defaults taken): window is fixed from the input's largest non-zero unit before rounding; a carry may leave a higher unit than the window start, which is simply printed ("86399, 2 -> 1d"). Validation of `max_units` precedes any other work. Bool/float `max_units` left unspecified.
+- Oracles: goldens come from the requester's examples (independent of the code); AC-007 is a property/differential sweep via arithmetic rounding of the input.
+- Step 4.6 spec-validator: not dispatched (light lane, `irreversible_decisions: []`).
